16. Required interactions and frontend behavior
Although the screenshot is a static representation, the interface should be implemented as a functional application rather than a collection of decorative elements.
Component	Expected functionality
Add Farm	Opens farm creation form
Search	Filters farms dynamically
All Farms	Filters by farm grouping
All Status	Filters by health status
Sort	Changes table sorting
List View	Displays the table
Grid View	Displays farm cards
Farm Name	Opens farm details
Verification Badge	Displays verified state
Status Badge	Displays farm health
Alert Count	Opens farm alerts
Three-dot Menu	Opens contextual actions
Table Row	Can navigate to farm details

Search behavior
Search should match:
- Farm name.
- Location.
- Active crop.
- Farm status.
Filtering should occur without a full page refresh.
Sorting behavior
Sorting should support:
- Last updated.
- Alphabetical farm name.
- Largest area.
- Smallest area.
- Most fields.
- Highest alert count.
Grid view
When grid view is selected, the table should be replaced by a responsive grid of farm cards.

The grid cards should reuse the same dark glassmorphism visual system.

17. Responsive implementation
The screenshot is a desktop reference, but the implementation should not be hardcoded to one screen resolution.
Large desktop: 1600 px and above
- Four statistics cards in one row.
- Full toolbar in one row.
- Full-width table.
- All nine table columns visible.
Medium desktop: 1024–1599 px
- Four cards if space permits, otherwise two columns.
- Toolbar controls can wrap.
- Table may use horizontal scrolling.
Tablet: 768–1023 px
- Statistics cards in a two-column grid.
- Search input spans most of the available width.
- Filters can move to a second toolbar row.
- Table uses horizontal scrolling.
Mobile: below 768 px
- Header becomes vertically arranged.
- Add Farm button remains accessible.
- Statistics become a two-column or single-column layout.
- Search occupies full width.
- Filters become horizontally scrollable or collapsible.
- Table can transform into individual farm cards.
- Action menus remain accessible.
Do not simply shrink the desktop table until its contents become unreadable.

18. Important pixel-level visual details
These details are particularly important for matching the reference.
1. The page background must remain almost black, with green atmospheric illumination.
2. The decorative foliage must be large, partially cropped, and positioned behind the UI.
3. The page title must be significantly larger than every other heading.
4. The logo must use a translucent rounded-square container.
5. The Add Farm button must be the brightest interactive element in the header.
6. All four statistics cards must have identical dimensions.
7. Each statistic card must have a different agricultural photographic background.
8. The cards must have a dark overlay so that the white text remains readable.
9. The search input must be substantially wider than the dropdowns.
10. All toolbar controls must have the same vertical height.
11. The table must have a large rounded outer container.
12. The table header must be separated from the data using a subtle horizontal line.
13. The farm thumbnail must appear before the farm name.
14. Farm names must be bold and locations must be displayed underneath.
15. Crop illustrations must be visually distinct from the text labels.
16. Healthy badges must use green.
17. Attention badges must use amber.
18. Alerts must use yellow when present and mint green when absent.
19. Every row must have consistent height and vertical alignment.
20. Every action button must have the same dimensions and corner radius.
21. The interface must have no unnecessary white surfaces.
22. Borders must be subtle rather than excessively bright.
23. The glass effect must be visible without making the interface look foggy.
24. Shadows should be soft, wide, and low-opacity.
25. Icons should have consistent stroke weight and visual scale.

